entry.summary:
Introduction
Starting from Bun v1.3.12, a new experimental API called Bun.Webview was introduced. It enables simple browser automation and can partially replace tools like Playwright. Pretty exciting, so I gave it a try. For macOS users, Bun.Webview can directly use the system’s native WebKit as the backend. On Windows and Linux, Chrome can be used as the backend via: const view = new Bun.WebView({ backend: "chrome" });
According to the Bun documentation, Bun searches for Chrome in the following order: The path provided in backend: { type: "chrome", path: "..." }
The BUN_CHROME_PATH environment variable $PATH (google-chrome-stable, google-chrome, chromium-browser, chromium, brave-browser, microsoft-edge, chrome) Common installation directories Playwright cache (~/Library/Caches/ms-play…
